Just a silly question, if this device has a 128 MiB SPI NAND why is ubi limited to 64 MiB?  Is the layout definition not incorrect in limiting it to 64 MiB - https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/blob/1df56d02cfe369cd1bfa61ddb009d645bbb6cadf/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7981b-cudy-m3000-v1.dts#L8
			partition@5c0000 {
				label = "ubi";
				reg = <0x05c0000 0x4000000>;

Compared to the xiaomi-redmi-router-ax6s which also only have a 128 MiB but in its layout allocate all of the remainder of the nand to ubi - https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/blob/1df56d02cfe369cd1bfa61ddb009d645bbb6cadf/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7622-xiaomi-redmi-router-ax6s.dts#L13
			partition@340000 {
				label = "ubi";
				reg = <0x340000 0x7280000>;
